    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112909" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χ χ,</span></b> 
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χεῖ</span></b>  (q.v.), τό, indecl., twenty-second letter of the Gr.
		alphabet, <i><span class="en">
			Pl.
			<u>Cra.</u>
			414b
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>Ti.</u>
			36b
		</span></i>. As numeral, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ́</span>
		=
		<i><span class="en">
			600
		</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">
			x'
		</span>
		=
		<i><span class="en">
			600
		</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
			000
		</span></i>: but in Inscrr., X stands for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χίλιοι,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αι</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,</span>
		=
		<i><span class="en">
			1000
		</span></i>.</div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
